Adaptive macOS icon asset maintenance. The Icon Composer source keeps square unmasked layers, with system-dark and tintable Mono specializations. The legacy fallback is rendered into all standard macOS iconset slots and verified for structure, required sizes, RGBA PNG payloads, and transparent corners. CI originally failed before testing because checkout required PRIVATE_REPOS_TOKEN even though ready-agent-cog is public; an anonymous recursive clone proved no private credential is needed, so CI and release submodule checkouts now use actions/checkout default authentication. The PAT used by the automated runner-version PR workflow remains because it has a separate documented purpose.
